content.text:
The degradation traces to one fault: the network path between search and rate. I did not find a second fault that reached users.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p, count(*) n, approx_quantile(d,0.05) p05, approx_quantile(d,0.5) p50, approx_quantile(d,0.9) p90, min(d) mn, max(d) mx FROM (SELECT 'abn' p, duration/1e6 d FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client' UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', duration/1e6 FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client') GROUP BY p",
          "claim": "search→rate client calls rose from ~0.5 ms median to ~1.9 s median (p05 1.5 s) in the incident period."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration, 0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM (SELECT 'abn' p, * FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', * FROM normal_traces) WHERE (service_name='rate' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Server') OR (service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client') GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY 2,4,1",
          "claim": "rate's own server span p95 stays near 1 ms while the search client span p95 jumps to ~2.9 s."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "rate",
      "to": "search",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, approx_quantile(duration, 0.95)/1e6 p95_ms, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='search' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Server') OR (service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client') GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "search's server span for Nearby inherits the ~2.9 s p95 from its rate client span, while rate itself stays fast."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, approx_quantile(duration, 0.95)/1e6 p95_ms, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' AND attr_span_kind='Server') OR (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Client') GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "frontend's /hotels p95 rises from ~17 ms to ~2.85 s, matching the slow search.Search/Nearby client span it waits on."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

